---
title: How to Use Programs and Categories
description: >-
  Group projects into programs and categories, rename "Program" to your own
  word, and use them to filter, sort and report.
sidebar:
  order: 19
---
**Programs and categories are two ways to organize your projects. A program groups several projects under one owner, such as a client retainer or a product launch. A category tags what kind of project it is, such as SEO or Website. A project can be in one program and in several categories.**

Both are managed in **Settings → Global → Project Settings**.

### **Programs**

A program rolls up the status and health of the projects inside it.

1. Go to **Settings → Global → Project Settings → Project programs**.
1. Click **Create program**.
1. Enter a **Name** (for example "Website relaunch"), choose an **Owner**, and optionally add a **Description** and a **Color**.
1. Click **Save**.

The table lists each program with its **Owner**, how many **Projects** it has, how many are **Active** and how many are **Off track**. Use the **...** actions to **Edit**, **Archive** or **Delete** a program. Switch on **Show archived** to see archived ones, and **Unarchive** to bring one back. A program that still has projects cannot be deleted: move or archive its projects first.

You need the **Project Programs** permission to change programs.

#### **Rename "Program"**

If "Program" is not the word your team uses, rename it. Above the table on the **Project programs** tab there is a field named **Program**.

1. Type your own word, for example "Folder" or "Initiative".
1. Click **Save**.

The new word replaces "Program" in the app's English text, in filters, columns, reports and settings, and it is pluralized automatically ("Folders"). Leave the field blank and save to go back to **Program**. Screens shown in another language keep that language's own wording.

### **Categories**

1. Go to **Settings → Global → Project Settings → Category**.
1. Click **Add Category**, enter a name, pick a color and click **Save**.
1. Use the pencil to rename a category and the bin to delete it.

### **Put a Project in a Program or Category**

Open the project, go to **Settings → General**, and use the **Program** picker and the **Select Category** field. You can pick several categories. The change is saved with the form.

### **Where You Can Use Them**

- **Projects list.** Open **Columns** and turn on **Program** and **Category**. In **Filter**, pick a program or a category, and use the manager and client filters to narrow further. See [How to Manage Project In Taskip](/project-management/how-to-manage-project-in-taskip/).
- **My Tasks.** Group by **Program** or **Category**, or filter by them. See [How to Use My Tasks](/project-management/how-to-use-my-tasks/).
- **Reports.** The project reports can be narrowed to one program or category, and show a breakdown by each. See [How to Use Reports](/reports/how-to-use-reports/).
